+/*
+ * VP9 DSP functions for PowerPC AltiVec/VMX (8-bit): 8-tap sub-pixel motion compensation (put/avg, h/v/hv)
+ * and the 8- and 16-wide loop filters. Generic AltiVec: G4, G5 and e6500, 32- or 64-bit, big-endian; no VSX.
+ *
+ * Bit-exact with the C code in vp9dsp_template.c:
+ *  - MC: every VP9 sub-pixel filter has non-negative centre taps (3, 4) and its six outer taps sum to at most
+ *    54*255 = 13770 in magnitude, so the outer taps accumulate exactly in 16 bits (modular vmladduhm) and the
+ *    two centre products are added with signed saturation. A saturated sum is outside [0, 32767] only when the
+ *    exact sum is too, and both clip to the same pixel after (s + 64) >> 7.
+ *  - Loop filter: the C arithmetic in 16-bit lanes (all intermediates fit in [-1020, 1020+]); the clip to
+ *    int8 range (av_clip_intp2(x, 7)) and to pixels are explicit.
+ *
